# Build output. The whole workspace shares one, so one rule covers ten crates.
/target/

# `cargo package` and `cargo publish` write here; the tarballs are artefacts of
# a release, not part of one.
**/*.crate

# Backtraces and profiler output.
*.profraw
perf.data*
flamegraph.svg

# Editors and desktop environments. Kept short on purpose: a repository is not
# the place to enumerate everybody's tools, and a global gitignore is.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# `cargo release` writes this while it works and removes it afterwards; a
# leftover means a run was interrupted.
Cargo.toml.orig

/RELEASE-CHECKLIST.md
